  "finalText": "Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n**Bug:** `runCli` in `commands.ts` had no `catch` block. When `runner.run()` threw an exception (e.g., CLI binary not found, timeout), `client.lastBuildError` was never set and no error notification was shown. The `finally` block's `refreshAll()` still updated the status bar, but it rendered \"no index\" (or stale counts from a prior build) instead of \"build failed\" — leaving the user with a misleading \"not ready\" state after the run had actually finished.\n\n**Fix (2 files, small and scoped):**\n\n1. **`apps/extension/src/commands.ts:205-208`** — Added a `catch` block that captures the runner exception, records it in `client.lastBuildError`, and shows an error notification. The existing `finally` block then runs `refreshAll()` → `statusBar.render()`, which now picks up the error and displays \"build failed\" with the exception message in the tooltip.\n\n2. **`apps/extension/tests/commands.test.ts`** — Added a test (\"shows 'build failed' when the runner throws\") that verifies the status bar transitions from \"indexing…\" to \"build failed\" when the runner throws, that `lastBuildError` is set, and that an error notification is shown.",
